# 2026-08-28 (HackMD review G): the rules below were added ONE PATH AT A TIME,
# five times, each after a new package directory appeared. build_submission.MIX
# and build_submission.SHIPPED.bak were never covered, and any future
# build_submission.E would not be either -- the trap re-arms itself every time
# the package moves. This glob covers every current and future variant, so the
# per-path rules below are now redundant (kept only for their reasoning).
build_submission*/** -text

# core.autocrlf is true in this repo, so a checkout on Windows rewrites LF to
# CRLF in the working tree. For most files that is harmless. For the submission
# package it is not: the package's IDENTITY is op_wrapper.py's md5 (the tar's own
# md5 is not reproducible -- gzip embeds an mtime), every handoff verifies against
# that md5, and a checked-out copy with CRLF would hash differently while looking
# correct. Mark the package byte-exact in both directions.
build_submission/** -text
bin/constructive_linux -text
*.exe -text
*.pkl -text
*.tar.gz -text

# L131 fix package (built + verified 2026-08-16, NOT uploaded). Same reasoning as
# build_submission/ above: its identity is op_wrapper.py's md5
# (2967efb6876f70685a18e1a160644fdd) and a CRLF rewrite on checkout would hash
# differently while looking correct. The pattern above does NOT cover this path.
build_submission.L131FIX/** -text

# L136 fix package (built + verified 2026-08-16, NOT uploaded). Same reasoning
# as build_submission/ above; the pattern there does NOT cover this path.
build_submission.L136FIX/** -text

# L245 no-vendor STANDBY package (built 2026-08-26, NOT uploaded). Same
# reasoning as build_submission/ above: its six graded files must stay
# byte-identical to the shipped package and a CRLF rewrite on checkout would
# hash differently while looking correct.
build_submission.NOVENDOR/** -text

# D variant (the artefact actually uploaded on 2026-08-26, vendor/ removed).
# Same reasoning as build_submission/ above: its identity is op_wrapper.py's
# md5 (1c326784de7cd9246cd1f380e2842668) and core.autocrlf=true would rewrite it
# to CRLF on checkout, changing the hash while the package still looks correct.
# The patterns above do NOT cover this path.
build_submission.D/** -text
